        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "7 months ago",
        "text": "No wonder they’re volunteers—they have no idea what theyre doing, wrong dates, misinformation about the area, the time and the age group. I signed for competitive and got recreative.\n\nIn conclusion, just don’t waste ur money here",
        "time": 1752354376,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Kaline Della-Malva",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107889897234715257244/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJl13XtkwDitlS-K2tuWUpm50xDQ7XgkFrt_jxZ7CIpsFxggg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "a year ago",
        "text": "U6 very unorganized for the amount of almost 300$ per child. Most teams dont have a coach and the first e-mails saying where and when the first game/practice would be were both wrong. When we got to the field the FC 3Lacs monitors told us that my sons team wasnt even supposed to play/practice that day despite it being clearly written that he was in 2 seperate e-mails from their administration. Now we have the app which doesnt tell you who's playing who and when you get to the field you have to go find a monitor to ask which field your kids team is playing on every game. The kids are not being monitored properly once games get going and it becomes complete chaos, pushing,shoving, etc etc. Each team needs a real coach to teach these young kids the basic of the game. I cant help but wonder each time what exactly costs 300$ for this? a jersey , ball and shorts? I dont understand scapegoating the parents into coaching most of your league when it costs 300$ per child. Not to mention the girls at the field are not super friendly or helpful. From what i hear this is a big step up from previous years where it was even MORE unorganized which is mind boggling. Good thing they're just young kids and just there to have fun regardless!",
        "time": 1717162975,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Joel Langlois",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109968149923089880242/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIaP12H7LJQSgHKfIV9vkiCP_zqYxOhVjkwYH7-kIMOzlof4Q=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 2,
        "relative_time_description": "3 years ago",
        "text": "First year registering my kid.    This organisation is horrible.    Refs are badly trained and clearly not supported,  and that's at a low houseleague level.   Weekend practices are a joke,  run by kids with no support or game plan!  Drills are ankle breakers or useless.    The icing on the cake,   they canceled the last game of the year because it was raining with lighting and thunder 20 minutes before the match!   At kickoff time it was all done yet no match!\n\nNot a great first soccer experience,   look forward to something better somewhere else",
        "time": 1661117094,
